From 3e1599f14e360f45512d9ad98222a0ab3e86c86c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:25:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] status bar: the ctx denominator is the live shared-pool
 share, not the static profile window
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two main sessions on one 451,264-token shared KV pool rendered
"ctx 175K/393.2K" and "ctx 234K/393.2K" -- the static profile context_length,
786,432 tokens of claimed window between them -- while the broker was
granting each of them 196,608. Nothing on either bar said they were sharing
anything.  [measured]

This is the same class of defect as patch 0001, one layer down. 0001 fixed a
figure that was read from the shared backend and labelled as though it were
the session's own. Here the figure is the session's own and the DENOMINATOR is
the lie: a percentage against a window the session will never be allowed to
fill.

A new module reads the document the pool broker publishes (share-bounded since
patch 0003) and turns it into what the bar divides by:

  ctx 40K/196.6K  | [##........] 20% | 2 mains, 451.3K pool
  ctx 40K/401.4K  | [#.........] 10% | 1 main,  451.3K pool
  ctx 175K/393.2K | [####......] 44% | 2 mains, 451.3K pool, share 196.6K (over)

The ceiling is the GRANT when the grant can be adopted without forcing a
compaction -- the same footprint test the compressor applies -- and otherwise
the window the session genuinely holds. So a grandfathered session is shown
honestly rather than pegged, and no window is lowered anywhere by a display.
A revocable loan is labelled on both sides.

DISPLAY ONLY, and the tests enforce it. It never writes, never probes the
backend, and never calls get_allowance(), which may refresh over the network
on the UI thread. 64 us per repaint: one stat() plus a parse, and only when
the broker has rewritten the file.  [measured] It degrades to the static
configured window when the document is absent, stale (>90 s, matching the
broker's own VRAM-sample age ceiling), or published by a peer old enough that
its ceilings are not share-bounded.

A frozen compressor in the test fixture turns any write from the display path
into a failure, and the ceiling tests drive the broker's real
derive_window_ceilings() for the 1/2/3-main splits, the loan pair, and a
1,310,720-token pool -- so the display cannot drift from the thing it
displays.

BASE: the tree left by patch 0007 (see BASELINE.md).

PUBLISHED FORM. A private backend address becomes 127.0.0.1, two live
process ids become synthetic ones, and an internal pane reference is
generalised.

